<!--
PILOT-LITE labeling config v2 (taxonomy v1.1a, pilot protocol v1.1b; layout revised 2026-11-25, compacted the same evening: groups flow inline and wrap, small titles, tight buttons so the label area and the diagram fit one screen).
Same classes, same per-box fields and relations as label_studio_config_lite.xml. Only the label-button
area changed: classes are grouped by treatment stage in separate rows with a group title, rare groups
(anaerobic wastewater reactor sub-types; full-subset-only classes) sit in collapsible panels, and hotkeys
are reduced to the ten most frequent units (digits) plus six very frequent helpers; every other label AND every Choice carries hotkey=" " (a space), which is the only way to stop Label Studio from auto-assigning letters (it otherwise gives choices keys like v b y o a k n m that collide with tool keys) (letters that do not
collide with Label Studio's own tool keys: b e h k m o p r u v w are reserved by the tool).
Exports are unchanged: every box is still a "rectanglelabels" result; s17/s19/s22 do not depend on the
tag name (from_name differs per group).
  * tasks 1-20  : FULL  (also arrowhead boxes and every text box -> open the last panel)
  * tasks 21-60 : LITE  (units, zones, io terminals, junctions, instruments; text boxes only for generic/unknown)
-->
<View>
  <Style>
    .ls-root { font-family: "Noto Sans KR", sans-serif; }
    .lsf-labels, .lsf-labels__list { padding: 0 !important; margin: 0 !important; }
    .lsf-label { margin: 1px 2px !important; padding: 1px 6px !important; font-size: 12px !important; line-height: 18px !important; }
    .lsf-label__hotkey { font-size: 10px !important; }
    .lsf-collapse .ant-collapse-header, .ant-collapse-header { padding: 2px 8px !important; font-size: 11px !important; }
    .ant-collapse-content-box { padding: 2px 6px !important; }
    .attrs sup { display: none !important; }   /* hides the empty "[ ]" left by hotkey=" " on choices */
  </Style>

